hey david do you think that donald  trump's new tone around coronavirus  taking it more seriously and wearing or  carrying around the mask is going to  help him turn the election around  i i don't think so no i mean i think  it's too little too late you know  for the first four or five months of  coronavirus in the united states  trump continued to say everything's fine  refuse to wear a mask  masks are you know it's your choice you  can wear it or not wear it or whatever  we have 15 cases it'll soon go to zero  etc etc etc in the last 10 to 14 days  we saw trump with a mask out in public  he keeps it in his suit pocket  during his coronavirus press briefings  to be able to pull it out like a prop  at any time he has actually said some  things that are more sober like it could  get worse before it gets  better and on and on and on will this  turn around the election for donald  trump  i don't believe so um i don't believe so  because  number one the cat is sort of out of the  bag from the standpoint of coronavirus  even if indeed the trump administration  is now covering up  cases since the changeover from  reporting data to the cdc  instead reporting data to health and  human services we covered that earlier  this week  people know that they're unemployed  people know that their friends are  unemployed people know the economy is a  catastrophe people  disapprove of trump's handling of racial  issues which is the third most important  issue going into november so i think  trump putting a mask on now  and saying this is tough is simply not  going to be  enough now could it still be important  as far as keeping people safe in other  words will trump supporters start  wearing masks because trump has worn a  mask  i seriously hope so because that is one  of the most important things that we can  do we covered on a bonus show earlier  this week  there's a lot of hygiene theater you  know restaurants announcing we're going  to close an hour early  to spray with some disinfectant the  entire  restaurant or whatever there's really no  evidence that significant contagion is  happening through surfaces  in that way you know cleaning tables and  seeding surfaces between guests  uh should be more than enough so there's  like hygiene theater stuff that does not  really seem to hold down contagion  wearing a mask does wearing a mask when  you're indoors  avoiding crowds that's the stuff that  really matters and so  if trump carrying his mask around helps  more trump supporters feel okay  putting on a mask then that's great and  i would be crazy to oppose that and i  don't oppose it  now there's one other component to this  it is possible that trump wearing a mask  and then more people wearing masks as a  result will  increase the number of people that feel  comfortable going and voting in person  in november maybe there were people in  november who maybe were going to stay  home  but now we're going to go out now i'm  thinking of democrats  what i mean is the following if you're a  trump supporter  and you're already not paying attention  to masks you're going to go out and vote  in person in november  if you're a democrat and you care about  masks and they aren't mandatory or a lot  of people aren't wearing them  you might stay home because others don't  plan to wear a mask  you seeing more republicans wearing  masks  might make you as a democrat more  comfortable going out to vote in  november  and that would be great it would be  great if trump wearing a mask  increases everybody's mass compliance  which makes more democrats feel  comfortable  going out and safely voting in november  if the death toll goes down  significantly that may actually be what  helps trump  the most and the mask wearing could be  part of it but it's a long path  right the mask wearing you need eight to  ten weeks to flatten the case curve  it's about another 15-20 days to deal  with the deaths  and then we're at election day so i just  don't know that the timing 